maria_dev: Trying to run the new JS worker example on Cloudflare and it dies with `ReferenceError: require is not defined` and `Cannot find module 'fs'`. Example still bundles node-fetch and Buffer.

samir_dx: CF Workers are ESM only and no Node built-ins. We need an edge build that uses globalThis.fetch and Web Crypto.

ida_engineer: Quick local patch: set package.json to \"type\": \"module\", replace require() with import, and accept apiKey via constructor instead of process.env. Also remove Buffer usage.

maria_dev: Typescript still fails because our index.d.ts references NodeJS.ReadableStream and Buffer. Worker projects error during tsc.

alex_docs: Proposal: produce dual outputs and types: dist/edge.esm.js + dist/node.cjs.js and dist/types/edge/*.d.ts and dist/types/node/*.d.ts. Update package.json exports to map import->edge, require->node.

samir_dx: Add runtime helper isEdge = typeof globalThis.process === 'undefined' && typeof globalThis.fetch === 'function' and accept injected fetch/getSecret.

ida_engineer: I sketched an edge adapter: ```js
export function createEdgeClient({ apiKey, fetchImpl = globalThis.fetch }){
  return async (payload)=>{
    const r = await fetchImpl('https://api.../v1/generate',{method:'POST',headers:{Authorization:`Bearer ${apiKey}`},body:JSON.stringify(payload)});
    if(!r.ok) throw new Error('upstream error');
    return r.json();
  }
}
```

ci-bot: build:example-worker failed 1.06. size 1.07MB > 1MB limit.

maria_dev: We need to drop polyfills and heavy libs. Remove any Buffer polyfill and avoid bundling node-fetch.

alex_docs: Action items: 1) PR from @ida_engineer with edge adapter + example changes, 2) @samir_dx to implement dual-build and export map, 3) add edge types and update README, 4) add CI step to bundle with wrangler/tsc --lib dom to catch regressions.

samir_dx: I'll handle the exports and runtime detection. ida please optimize bundle size. alex will add CI.

maria_dev: Thanks — once these land I'll re-run the customer sample. :thumbsup:
